  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "An owner converting an **independent upper-upscale hotel** usually begins with the major **soft-brand collections**, which preserve much of the property’s name, design, and local identity while adding distribution and loyalty-system access.\n\n### Most common shortlist\n\n| Parent company | Collection/brand | Typical fit |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Marriott** | **Autograph Collection** | Often the first Marriott option considered for distinctive, full-service upper-upscale hotels |\n|  | **Tribute Portfolio** | Independent, character-driven lifestyle hotels; generally somewhat more flexible than Autograph |\n| **Hilton** | **Curio Collection by Hilton** | Core upper-upscale competitor to Autograph and Unbound |\n|  | **Tapestry Collection by Hilton** | More appropriate when the property falls closer to upscale than upper-upscale |\n| **Hyatt** | **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt** | Historic, iconic, resort, or story-rich upper-upscale and luxury properties |\n|  | **Destination by Hyatt** | Particularly relevant for destination resorts and experiential properties |\n| **IHG** | **Vignette Collection** | Higher-end upper-upscale/luxury lifestyle hotels retaining a strong independent identity |\n| **Accor** | **MGallery Hotel Collection** | Boutique, design-led upper-upscale hotels, especially in international markets |\n| **Choice/Radisson** | **Radisson Individuals** | Explicitly positioned for upper-upscale independent conversion projects |\n| **Wyndham** | **Registry Collection Hotels** | Upper-upscale/luxury independent resorts and distinctive urban hotels |\n| **Sonesta** | **Classico Collection by Sonesta** | Upper-upscale soft brand emphasizing high-touch service, local cuisine, and refined interiors |\n| **BWH Hotels** | **WorldHotels Elite** or **BW Premier Collection** | Alternatives for owners seeking greater operating independence or a lower-cost affiliation structure |\n\nMarriott specifically presents Autograph, Tribute and Luxury Collection as operating platforms for independent hotels. Hilton identifies Curio as upper-upscale, while Hyatt directly lists Autograph, Luxury Collection and Curio as competitors to Unbound. ([hotel-development.marriott.com](https://www.hotel-development.marriott.com/brands/premium-brands?utm_source=openai))\n\nOther credible conversion candidates include MGallery, Radisson Individuals, Registry Collection and Classico. MGallery is positioned as upper-upscale; Radisson Individuals is designed for upper-upscale independent conversions; Wyndham calls Registry an upper-upscale soft brand; and Sonesta positions Classico against Curio, Autograph, Tribute and similar collections. ([group.accor.com](https://group.accor.com/en/news-stories/collection-brands-handwritten-emblems-mgallery?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Practical “core four”\n\nFor a typical U.S. upper-upscale urban or resort asset, the initial competitive process most often centers on:\n\n1. **Autograph Collection**\n2. **Curio Collection**\n3. **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt**\n4. **Tribute Portfolio**\n\nThe list then expands based on positioning:\n\n- **Luxury-leaning:** Vignette, Luxury Collection, Registry Collection  \n- **Resort-oriented:** Destination by Hyatt, Unbound, Registry  \n- **International/boutique:** MGallery  \n- **More owner flexibility or lower affiliation cost:** Radisson Individuals, Classico, WorldHotels Elite, BW Premier Collection  \n- **Closer to upscale:** Tapestry, Ascend Hotel Collection, BW Premier Collection  \n\nThe best choice normally turns on the projected **net contribution after fees**, required property-improvement plan, key money, loyalty penetration in the market, contract term, territorial protection, and how much control the owner wants to retain over the hotel’s name, design, F&B and operating standards.",
